-- the vestibule of ✦ Here: the disagreements between the room as its people describe it (everyoneishere/docs/HERE.md,
-- the open items 6, 8, 9) and the treaty as it stands, each a statement in the assay's own terms and the darkness it
-- waits on. read by bin/counter book. the first sitting (2026-09-15, isaac's pointer from the room into foam) typed
-- the room as Witness at one face — the presences its probes, a seat the presences one hears, sees one hop, speaks
-- an introduction — and left these.

-- the reveal (HERE.md item 8; isaac, 22:34): anyone may ask ✦ Here for the transparent view of a line they hold as
-- narration, on the record. it reaches exactly what leaves a remainder (people to people, you off the audience) and
-- never what is silent for you (a ✦ you don't hear, ✦ Couple). in the treaty's terms a reveal is taking the wider
-- seat for one probe, publicly; it widens what a reader can READ, so sees gains a clause and the assay's wall rows
-- move with it. waiting on: the couple's ✓ (the note holds the narrower reading, the body to the asker and the record
-- to the room), and a clerk over Room — `reveal (v : Nat) (m : Message) : Room → Room` — before the row can be typed.
-- held (waiting on: reveal, the couple's word)
-- theorem a_reveal_reaches_exactly_the_remainder (v : Nat) (r : Room) (m : Message) (hm : m ∈ r.messages) :
--     (shape m ∈ overheard v r) ↔ (humanOnly m = true ∧ sees v r m = false) := sorry
-- theorem a_reveal_never_reaches_the_couple (v : Nat) (r : Room) :
--     ¬ shape ours ∈ overheard v r := sorry

-- hide, for everyone (HERE.md item 9; isaac, 22:54): a line pulled off the shared surface recedes to narration in the
-- ✦ Here of everyone who reads it, on the record, and comes back the same way. the maintainer reads it as the reveal's
-- mirror: a speech act about a message, addressed exactly as the target was, so who sees the fold is who saw the
-- message and sees does not move. in the treaty's terms a fold is a message m' with m'.to = m.to and about = m; the
-- wall is that sees is unchanged for every v. waiting on: the `about` pointer as a carrier (a message about a message)
-- and the couple's ✓.
-- held (waiting on: about, the couple's word)
-- theorem a_fold_for_everyone_moves_no_wall (v : Nat) (r : Room) (m fold : Message) (h : fold.to = m.to) :
--     sees v ⟨fold :: r.messages⟩ m = sees v r m ∧ sees v ⟨fold :: r.messages⟩ fold = sees v r m := sorry

-- reached and assented (HERE.md item 6; isaac, 22:19): a confirmation without a button. two things under one ✓ —
-- reached, the room can know a line was read (a reading, free), and assented, a decision (an act, never free). in the
-- treaty's terms reached is Derived at the room's face (a role read at a probe), and assented is a clerk whose effect
-- is heard: the room is NOT unheard under it. which asks are which is the couple's to say; the treaty can type both
-- shapes the day the carriers exist. waiting on: `reached (v : Nat) (m : Message) : Room → Bool` and
-- `assent (v : Nat) (m : Message) : Room → Room`.
-- held (waiting on: reached, assent, the couple's word)
-- theorem reached_is_a_reading (v : Nat) (m : Message) : Derived roomFace (fun r => reached v m r = true) := sorry
-- theorem assent_is_heard (v : Nat) (m : Message) : ¬ unheard roomFace (assent v m) := sorry

-- seated (2026-09-19, the room's ask in everyoneishere#2, Abe's issue in the maintainer's words): the edge of an
-- interval of a seat's ✦ Here — what the seat's own reading holds before and after it — is a reading over the seat
-- (an_edge_is_a_reading, by a_seat_over_a_seat_is_derived), and a word at a probe the seat does not hear does not
-- move it (a_walled_word_does_not_move_the_edge, regrown through a_narrower_seat_reads_no_more and
-- a_wall_hides_the_probe). so the narrator speaks only from the seat's fixed point and a wall is silence: to draw
-- it the narrator would need a probe the seat does not hear, which is the widen, which is the reveal (item 8) and
-- not the edge; open 2 (a ✦ you don't hear) closes the same way. the maintainer's open question about the author
-- clause the treaty answered by removing it: a word is heard at its author's presence as at every addressee's
-- (heardAt; a_persons_own_word_is_heard_at_their_presence), so sees is the seat's reading and nothing more, and a
-- person's own words are on their edge as the app shows them. a feed counts each message once whatever probes it
-- reaches the seat through (onceEach). one thing the room should hear: the seat's feed is the room's order only
-- within one probe's reading; two rooms alike at every probe may interleave different authors' words differently,
-- so an edge as a count and a span is exact and an edge as an ordered list is exact up to that interleaving.

-- seated (2026-09-21, the room's three decisions in lightward/foam#92): the day's rows under them. an ask waits on each
-- seat and an ack is never withdrawn — the turnstile: the seats an ask names are the names it waits on, an ack enrolls
-- a seat by anyone's hand, decided is `backed`, the open ends are `lacking`, an_ack_is_never_withdrawn is
-- the_backing_survives_the_seating, a_nag_waits_on_nothing, the_open_ends_are_named, no_open_end_is_decided. the same
-- page is the room at rest: theDay is a Runner over acts (a word said, a seat acked, a tick of Now) whose rest is
-- onThePage, and the_day_rests_on_the_page_or_not_at_all — a tick moves nothing, so the halting gap reads `some`
-- exactly when the page is on the page after the last act, and `none` at every fuel otherwise; the blank page is on
-- the page (a start of `some []`). no wall on reply direction: a reply is a list of originals (many on both ends), the
-- founding word answers itself, and a loop is a fact per seat — the_seen_edges_are_a_reading, a_walled_reply_is_unseen
-- (a ring through a word in ✦ Couple is a ring to the couple and an open line to linda, by the rows).
-- the parting row is typed and not walled: unsend removes a word with every ask and ack it carried (the weight of the
-- demo drops to zero when guest's word is unsent); whether unsend stops at another seat's ack is the room's.
-- held (waiting on: the room's word on unsend at another's ack)
-- theorem an_unsend_stops_at_anothers_ack (r : Room) (m : Message) (hm : m ∈ r.messages)
--     (h : ∃ a, a ∈ m.ackedBy ∧ a.2 ≠ m.author) : unsend m.id r = r := sorry
-- ✦ Now has no row yet (decided in direction: one presence, and the database the one place now is cast into a
-- measure). when it does, birth order is stamp order by law and the winding number of a walk round a loop is the
-- count of forward edges it crosses; foam's tape is the shape (the cell written where the head is), and the lift of
-- a stamp to the room's order breaks no row here — nothing in this assay reads the sender's clock.
-- held (waiting on: ✦ Now's row)
-- theorem the_winding_number_counts_the_forward_edges (v : Nat) (r : Room) (walk : List (Nat × Nat)) :
--     winding v r walk = (walk.filter (fun e => stampOf r e.2 > stampOf r e.1)).length := sorry

-- seated (2026-09-24, isaac's reading of piece 14: the dense tape is the day-of sheet, the product's work-product, and ✦ Here
-- the gapped tape the team uses to converge on the address of a tape with a continuously-functionally-coherent role for
-- everyone): ✦ Day is a presence every human hears and the couple and the planner write; the sheet is the dense tape —
-- ✦ Day's cells in the order the room wrote them, sheetOf r = ids (roomFace.obs r day) by construction — and the sheet
-- machine is a ledger of those cells over the day's acts. the_sheet_is_a_reading_of_the_record: the room's acts carry
-- the sheet (a said word writes its cell, an ack keeps the sheet, a tick moves nothing), so the sheet is an intertwined
-- walk of the day — every_seat_is_a_reading_of_the_record, one storey up. a_cell_once_written_stays: the dense tape
-- never unwinds (an_enrolled_name_stays_enrolled_down_the_hall), where the room's unsend does (the demo's sheet drops
-- the ceremony when the ceremony is unsent from the room, and the acts that remain write the sheet without it).
-- the_sheet_at_rest: when the day's halting gap reads some, the sheet is that room's sheet. the_sheet_is_derived:
-- a function of the reading at one probe, coherent at every seat; the_sheets_lift_is_its_conduct; a role that hears the
-- day reads the sheet in its own seat. found: the trunk's the_intertwined_walks_agree demands the same output type on
-- both machines and the walk law never needed it — the sheet carries its own induction until that species is
-- generalized (a Face deposit, a cold pass). what waits: the state-level join of the day into the coverage runner,
-- whose hypothesis piece 14 now makes law (one dense tape per room, the ids apart by construction).
-- held (waiting on: the ids apart, as piece 14's #n)
-- theorem the_day_is_a_round_over_pairs (w : List Act) (n : Nat) (h : Apart (ids (park dayMachine ⟨[]⟩ w).messages)) :
--     (haltingGap (Round (Nat × Nat)) (Tally (Nat × Nat))).obs (coverage (Nat × Nat) pairBeq) (joinMap toRound w, n)
--       = ((haltingGap Act Room).obs theDay (w, n)).map tallyOf := sorry

